{
  "_comment": "INDUSTRIAL: a twin work-light on a short mast - a base puck, a post, a crossbar and two lamp heads tilted thirty-five degrees down at the deck ahead. The lenses are the one bright material in the kit: flat warm white at low roughness, because the pipeline has no emissive and a pale low-rough face is what reads as a lit lamp against the dark steel. Not yellow and not a fourth accent - it is the lamp itself, the same move as the civilian kit's amber. The heads aim down +Z and the rule turns the piece OUTWARD, so a pair by a fitting reads as yard lighting rigged over the work face.",
